---
// Front page. The real homepage is Phase 3; until then this is a notice
// in house voice so that the masthead has somewhere to lead.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout mastheadAs="h1">
  <article class="notice">
    <p class="label label--accent">Notice to the Public</p>
    <h2>First Edition Delayed by Circumstances Entirely Within Our Control</h2>
    <p class="dek">
      The presses are warm, the editors are present, and the news has been asked to wait
      in the corridor until it is called.
    </p>
    <div class="rule-ornament" role="separator"><span class="ornament">&#x2767;&#xFE0E;</span></div>
    <p class="drop-cap">
      The Municipal Absurdist will commence publication shortly. A committee has been
      formed to determine how shortly, and a second committee has been formed to
      oversee the first. Both report excellent progress and have requested more chairs.
    </p>
    <p>
      In the interim, readers may inspect the type, rules, and ornaments in
      the <a href="/styleguide">Office of Typographical Standards</a>. Admission is free
      and the exits are clearly marked.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .notice {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .notice h2,
  .notice .dek,
  .notice .label {
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
